Spec: specs/000-foundation/spec.md (Logging: nothing writes plain text)
Why this approach: forbidigo on os.Stdout/os.Stderr, excluded by path+text for the two sanctioned places, so the zap-globals ban still applies inside internal/logging.
Verified by: a throwaway internal/throwaway/throwaway.go using fmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, ...), os.Stdout.WriteString(...) and log.Default().Println(...) gave 3 forbidigo findings; the same file in internal/logging/ and cmd/gateway/main.go gave only the log.Default finding. Deleted afterwards. setup-lint with a bogus version: curl 404, "golangci-lint install failed", make setup exits 2; a fresh install into a scratch BIN exits 0.
